textZh:
RRF 融合与“何时都走一遍”  // 只利用排名，不比较原始分数
 RRF(d) = Σ 1 / (k + rank_i(d))

 // rank_i(d)：文档 d 在第 i 个列表中的名次
 // k：平滑头部名次影响，常见示例 60，
 //    但必须在自己的评测集上验证 WHEN 什么时候多路并行反而合理？ ① Query 同时含 ID 与自然语言原因；② Router 置信度低且风险允许扩大召回；③ 高召回优先的离线调查；④ 构建评测基线比较路径贡献；⑤ 单一 Retriever 有已知盲区。 但必须设置： 并发上限 · 超时预算 · 权限过滤 · 去重融合 · 降级路径 · 成本权衡。 RRF 是候选融合，不是最终相关性证明 → 还需 Cross-Encoder / LLM Reranker → Evidence Validation。  成熟表达 Use the cheapest reliable route first, and expand retrieval only when the query or uncertainty requires it.

textEn:
RRF Fusion and “When to Run Every Path”  // Use ranks only; do not compare raw scores
 RRF(d) = Σ 1 / (k + rank_i(d))

 // rank_i(d): rank of document d in list i
 // k: smooths the impact of top ranks; 60 is a common example,
 //    但必须在自己的评测集上验证 WHEN When is multi-path parallel retrieval reasonable? ① The Query contains both an ID and a natural-language reason; ② Router confidence is low and risk allows broader recall; ③ an offline investigation prioritizes recall; ④ building evaluation baselines to compare path contribution; ⑤ a single Retriever has a known blind spot. But you must set: concurrency limits · timeout budgets · permission filtering · deduplication/fusion · degradation paths · cost trade-offs. RRF fuses candidates; it does not prove final relevance → still use Cross-Encoder / LLM Reranker → Evidence Validation.  Mature Answer Use the cheapest reliable route first, and expand retrieval only when the query or uncertainty requires it.

